# FDD 08 review — "08 - Interface and Integrations Setup". Ingested per
# abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md. This folder is NOT one FDD with one Addendum —
# it is 11 separate "Interface Design Document" (IDD) sub-documents, each describing one
# named external-system integration, plus a stray "TO BE DELETED 8.3, 8.9 - Data
# Warehouse" folder (an old, superseded "8.3 - Data Warehouse IDD.docx" with NO Addendum
# at all — genuinely replaced by the current "8.9 - CEPI Data Warehouse" doc; read in full,
# confirmed superseded, not converted). Each real sub-document DOES carry its own numbered
# "## Addendum" user-story section in "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I want..." form (all
# system-actor stories, no citizen-facing ones anywhere in this folder) — that Addendum,
# not the free-text interface-spec prose/JSON schemas/field-mapping tables above it, is
# the Requirement unit used below, consistent with every other FDD pass in this project.
#
# THE KEY QUESTION THIS PASS ANSWERS (per this review's own brief — FDD 02 and FDD 29 are
# both waiting on it): "Interface and Integrations Setup (8)" is NOT a missing bounded
# context and does NOT need a GAPS.md "whole area has no home" entry. It decomposes
# cleanly into external-system integrations that belong to FIVE different EXISTING
# bounded contexts, three of which already have real, load-bearing coverage for their
# piece of it:
#   - 8.1 EEM Interface + 8.1 Entity Directory Data Population -> organizations
#     (ext:EEMSystem + orgs:BatchJob_CepiNightlySync already exist and substantially
#     satisfy this — see Feature 8.1 below for a real mechanism-vs-mechanism discrepancy
#     found while checking the citation).
#   - 8.2 NASDTEC Ed ID Clearinghouse -> profpractice (ext:NASDTECSystem,
#     profp:Seq_ProcessNasdtecNightlyBatch, profp:Rule_NASDTECNightlyBatchProcessing
#     already exist and substantially satisfy this).
#   - 8.3 STARR Interface -> proflearning for the course-data half (starr:StarrSystem
#     already exists there); credentialing for the post-secondary-award-data half
#     (genuinely unmodeled — see Question_StarrAwardDataGapInCredentialing).
#   - 11.8 MTTC EdReports (Pearson) -> credentialing (asp:AssessmentProviderSystem,
#     cred:Op_ImportAssessmentResults, cred:Seq_ImportAssessmentResults already exist and
#     substantially satisfy the manual-upload half).
#   - 8.4 Data Hub, 8.5 CTEIS, 8.6 NexSys, 8.7 MSDS-TSDL, 8.8 Secure Site -> staffing
#     (the natural owner — every one of these moves staff/assignment/employment data by
#     Unique ID). NONE of the five has ANY corresponding Dependency, Sequence, or
#     ExternalSystem node anywhere in staffing-domain.ttl/staffing-sequences.ttl today —
#     this is a genuine, real coverage gap within an existing domain (not a "no home"
#     situation), so per CONVENTIONS.md new sd:ExternalSystem stubs for these five systems
#     are minted below, in THIS file (not staffing's own files, which this pass doesn't
#     own) so the Requirement/Annotation/Dependency machinery has something concrete to
#     point at; a future staffing-domain pass should fold them into
#     staffing-domain.ttl/staffing-sequences.ttl proper.
#   - 8.9 CEPI Data Warehouse: the one piece that turned out to be neither satisfied nor a
#     coverage gap at all — see the out-of-scope Annotation below. This is this pass's
#     single most important finding and the concrete resolution of what FDD 02 and FDD 29
#     were both pointing at.
#
# Skipped per CONVENTIONS.md: the free-text interface-spec fields (transmission protocol,
# environments, field-layout tables, sample JSON, generated C#/OpenAPI model dumps) above
# each Addendum — these are the IDD template's own boilerplate, not requirements, and are
# folded into sd:notes/sd:integrationNotes only where a specific field materially confirms
# or contradicts something. The "MORE Integrations.xlsx"/"MORE Integrations.md" workbook
# (a master list of ALL integrations across the whole solution, most already covered by
# other FDDs/domains) and "MORE Interfaces with other systems.msg" (an email) were read for
# context/cross-checking only, per this project's "skip non-docx unless load-bearing"
# rule — neither introduced a numbered requirement of its own. "Public Services_Teacher
# Information User Guide.docx" and "Interface Design document- Template.docx" (the blank
# template) were also read; the User Guide is REP/CTEIS/NexSys/MSDS's shared underlying
# API reference (corroborates the "same set of service endpoints... based on existing REP
# services" note found independently in 8.5's own IDD) and contributed no new requirements
# of its own. "11.8 MTTC" is numbered under Business Specification 11 (System Admin -
# Credentialing), not 8, but its source docx lives physically inside this FDD 8 folder —
# converted here rather than left out, per this project's practice of following where the
# source material actually sits.
#
# Review comments (word/comments.xml, extracted via unzip + a small node regex script,
# not python — python3 wasn't available in this environment): most across all 11
# sub-documents are pure "field is TBD, please fill in" editorial nagging from one
# reviewer (Caswell) with no requirement-level content — not transcribed individually.
# Two threads are substantial and modeled as standalone Annotations below: the CEPI Data
# Warehouse "is this story needed... not needed, suggesting to remove" rejection thread
# (Question_DataWarehouseOutOfScope — the headline finding) and the Data Hub
# direction-dispute thread (Question_DataHubFlowDirectionDisputed). The NASDTEC comment
# "we have to define this retention policy" independently corroborates
# profp:Question_NASDTECDataLifecycle (already on record from the profpractice domain
# pass) rather than raising new ground — not re-modeled as a duplicate Annotation.
#
# Embedded images: two sub-documents (8.1 EEM Interface IDD, 8.6 NexSys IDD) contain a
# couple of .emf (Enhanced Metafile) images each — checked via `unzip -l`. These IDDs are
# technical interface specs (protocol/schema/field-mapping documents), not UI-flow FDDs;
# .emf in this document type is almost always a pasted Office chart/table/logo fragment,
# not a wireframe, and the Read tool cannot render .emf directly. No wireframes/ subfolder
# is created for this file — there is no UI in scope anywhere in this FDD folder to
# wireframe; every story here is a system-to-system integration behavior.
#
# Numbering note: 8.9's own Addendum starts at 8.9.2 (no 8.9.1 exists anywhere in the
# document) — preserved as-is, not renumbered, consistent with this project's practice of
# keeping a source FDD's own literal numbering even when it's got a gap or collision.

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix cred:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:> .
@prefix profp: <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:> .
@prefix plrn:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:> .
@prefix orgs:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:organizations:> .
@prefix staff: <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:> .
@prefix rpt:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:> .
@prefix ext:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:> .
@prefix starr: <urn:solutiondesign:instance:starr:> .
@prefix asp:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:assessmentprovider:> .

