    sd:notes "8 review comments, editorial (TBD fields, scheduling, a suggestion to note STARR's annual collection cadence) — no requirement-level content beyond what the Addendum itself states." .
staff:Fdd08_4DataHubDoc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "fdd" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/08 - Interface and Integrations Setup/8.4 - Data Hub/8.4 - Data Hub IDD.docx" ;
    sd:notes "33 review comments (by far the most of any sub-document in this folder) — most are 'reasonable use case for the API'/'values provided'/'endpoint added' resolution notes on the HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS table's 20 Ed-Fi Identities API use cases (skipped per CONVENTIONS.md as duplicative of the Addendum, same as every other FDD's HLS table). Two threads are substantive and modeled as standalone Annotations below: a live data-flow-direction dispute (Question_DataHubFlowDirectionDisputed) and an unresolved Mi-Key-vs-MiEdWorkforce ownership question (Question_DataHubMiKeyOwnershipUnconfirmed). A third comment ('Potential to source from CTEIS in the future, but not initial use case') confirms the Career-Cluster/CIP-Code fields in the HLS table are explicitly future/deferred, not part of the current 8.4.1-8.4.5 Addendum scope." .
staff:Fdd08_5CteisDoc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "fdd" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/08 - Interface and Integrations Setup/8.5 - CTEIS Interface/8.5 - CTEIS Interface IDD.docx" ;
